final ps = Process.runSync('ps', ['-ax', '-o', 'pid=']);
skip: ps.exitCode != 0 → hmm, dynamic skip inside test = throw Skip.
``
I'll restructure: if ps fails → `throw Skip('ps unavailable')`... Actually simplest: the provisioning test — assert contains('$pid'); the ANCESTOR part: assert that every element is a positive int > 1... loses ancestor semantics. CI boxes have ps; the failure mode is theoretical. Keep it simple: contains(pid) + length>1 guarded by ps success:

```dart
final ps = Process.runSync('ps', ['-ax', '-o', 'pid=,ppid=']);
final exported = ...;
expect(exported, contains('$pid'));
if (ps.exitCode == 0) expect(exported.length, greaterThan(1));
``
That keeps the meaningful assertion on every normal host. Apply.

